  "description": "TANJAX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P 1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C55 H111 Cr3 Gd3 N3 O27,3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.350-4.045 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.10-113.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C55H117Cr3Gd3N3O30. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
